<Configuration>
  <!-- Testing the published kit the way a stranger meets it.

       This is not the sandbox for playing (SoA.wsb). Nothing of the project is
       mapped in - no tools, no Python, no dgVoodoo already beside the game, no
       registry settings. A clean Windows, a plain installation of the game, and
       the zip exactly as it comes off the release page. If the kit needs
       anything that is only on the development machine, this is where it shows.

       The game folder was mapped read only at first, so that the test could not
       change the copy it was given. It is writable now by request; see the note
       on the mapping below for what that costs. -->

  <!-- On, by request. The playing sandbox keeps it off - the game has not
       needed it since the GameSpy servers died in 2014 - and this one does not
       need it either, so what it is for is the tester: fetching something into
       the sandbox, or watching what the launcher does with a network available.

       One consequence worth knowing. The playing sandbox writes the dead
       GameSpy hosts into `hosts` because otherwise the game's version check at
       startup sits waiting for a timeout. This sandbox deliberately does not,
       since a stranger's machine would not have it either - so if the game
       takes half a minute to come up, that is what it is doing. -->
  <Networking>Enable</Networking>
  <ClipboardRedirection>Enable</ClipboardRedirection>
  <AudioInput>Disable</AudioInput>
  <VideoInput>Disable</VideoInput>
  <PrinterRedirection>Disable</PrinterRedirection>

  <VGpu>Enable</VGpu>
  <MemoryInMB>8192</MemoryInMB>
  <ProtectedClient>Disable</ProtectedClient>

  <MappedFolders>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>F:\Games\SoA-KitTest</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\Given</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>true</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
    <!-- Writable, by request. It is the host's clean installation, so anything
         written here outlives the sandbox and the next run no longer starts
         from a clean one - which is exactly how the last clean copy stopped
         being clean. Rebuilding it is two minutes:
             build-package.ps1 -Variant vanilla -->
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>F:\Games\SoA-Vanilla\Game</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\Retail</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>false</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
  </MappedFolders>

  <LogonCommand>
    <Command>C:\Given\kit-test.cmd</Command>
  </LogonCommand>
</Configuration>
